9. What are embeddings?
Ans: A mathematical representation of a token. that stored on vector database.

10. How do embedding models work?
Ans: An embedding model converts text into a numerical vector that captures its semantic meaning.
      Similar pieces of text are mapped to vectors that are close to each other in the embedding space.
      In RAG, we generate embeddings for document chunks and user queries, then use vector similarity to retrieve the most relevant chunks.”
      Text → Embedding Model → Vector → Similarity Search → Relevant Content

